{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"Normal rules are in effect for the Sudoku puzzle, with a unique twist. The numbers in the cells contained within grey lines have a special condition, they must add up to the figures in the corner. This means that the sum of the numbers in these cells will be equal to the number in the corner, providing an additional layer of complexity to the puzzle.\n\n\n \nAddition to the standard rules, the numbers in each shape formed by grey lines must be unique. No number can be repeated within each of these shapes, which will require careful planning and attention to detail to solve the puzzle. The shapes formed by grey lines will have a distinct set of numbers, with no overlaps or duplicates.\n\n\n \nThe Sudoku puzzle is a challenging and engaging activity that requires logical thinking and problem-solving skills. The unique twist of the grey lines and corner figures adds an extra layer of complexity, making it more difficult to solve. However, this also makes it more rewarding, as the sense of accomplishment will be greater when the puzzle is finally completed.\n\n\n \nTo access the completed puzzle, readers can buy next week’s Observer Digital Edition. This will provide the solution to the puzzle, allowing readers to check their work and see how the numbers fit together. The completed puzzle will be a useful resource for those who are struggling to solve it, or for those who want to verify their answers.\n\n\n \nThe Sudoku puzzle is a fun and challenging activity that can be enjoyed by people of all ages and skill levels. With its unique twist and complex rules, it provides a stimulating and engaging way to exercise the mind and improve problem-solving skills. Whether you are a seasoned puzzle solver or just starting out, the Sudoku puzzle is a great way to challenge yoursel